{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>The young men.</b> My servants who went with me — and also Aner, Eshkol, and Mamre, etc. Even though my servants entered the battle, as it says ״הוּא וַעֲבָדָיו וַיַּכֵּם״, and Aner and his companions stayed by the baggage to guard — even so, they shall take their share. And from him David learned, who said ״כְּחֵלֶק הַיֹּרֵד בַּמִּלְחָמָה וּכְחֵלֶק הַיֹּשֵׁב עַל הַכֵּלִים יַחְדָּו יַחֲלֹקוּ״ (1 Samuel 30), and therefore it says ״וַיְהִי מֵהַיּוֹם הַהוּא וָמָעְלָה וַיְשִׂימֶהָ לְחֹק וּלְמִשְׁפָּט״ (ibid.), and it does not say 'and onward' — because the ordinance had already been given in the days of Abram."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:44.859669341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}